{
  "dom_id": "step-q125637",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/e60f7c0adc3e2ec8daa3203564c31bf660e6eca7e6394955cc73133ac3673ed5.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\u222e}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$",
  "worked_solution": "The circulation $\u0393$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/a8010db8481768cb61d0734dcfc97eed646441ab265c4928d06d274ef0e1c1dd.png)\n\nSo, ${\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/be263d706bfc3ef205be37aaed85d4984d3739d53cdaadb8cba88e3d5196ce93.png)\n\nSo, ${\u222e}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
